# DroidNode toolchain locations -- TEMPLATE, safe to commit.
#
# Copy this file to `toolchain.env.local` and fill in the paths for your machine:
#     Copy-Item toolchain.env.example toolchain.env.local
#
# `toolchain.env.local` is gitignored on purpose: real absolute paths never
# reach the repository. Scripts read it in this order:
#     1. toolchain.env.local   (this file's copy -- wins over everything)
#     2. variables already set in your environment
#     3. auto-detection        (PATH, %LOCALAPPDATA%, rustup defaults, ...)
#
# Format: one KEY=VALUE per line, `#` starts a comment, quotes are stripped.
# Only set what you need; a missing entry falls through to the next step.

# --- Rust (rustup home + cargo home) ------------------------------
# RUSTUP_HOME=
# CARGO_HOME=

# --- JDK 17 -------------------------------------------------------
# JAVA_HOME=

# --- Android SDK + NDK --------------------------------------------
# ANDROID_HOME=
# ANDROID_NDK_HOME=

# --- Go (used by the SPDY sidecar build) --------------------------
# GO=
# GOPATH=
# GOCACHE=

# --- Optional tools -----------------------------------------------
# GRADLE_HOME=
# MINGW_HOME=
# PYTHON=
# ADB=

# --- Optional: one root for all toolchains -------------------------
# When set, any unset variable above falls back to a conventional
# subdirectory of this root:
#     <root>\rust\rustup-home   <root>\rust\cargo-home
#     <root>\jdk                <root>\android-sdk
#     <root>\go                 <root>\gradle
#     <root>\mingw64
# Per-tool variables always take precedence over this root.
# A repo-local `toolchain/` directory is also gitignored if you prefer
# to keep everything inside the checkout.
# DROIDNODE_TOOLCHAIN_ROOT=
